WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.620
The drone's four buttons

2
00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:09.813
are the columns of A: u, v, w and s.

3
00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:14.913
Every target it can reach lies in one plane

4
00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:19.900
b one minus b two plus b three equals zero.

5
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.307
Lay that plane flat

6
00:00:22.307 --> 00:00:26.934
and measure every point in steps of u and v.

7
00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:31.561
Then u is one step across, v is one step up

8
00:00:31.561 --> 00:00:36.086
w, which is two u plus v, sits at two, one

9
00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:38.862
and s, which is v minus u

10
00:00:38.862 --> 00:00:41.330
sits at minus one, one.

11
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.715
How many buttons does the drone really need

12
00:00:45.807 --> 00:00:48.192
to reach a target like the

13
00:00:48.283 --> 00:00:50.759
delivery point at one, one?

14
00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:54.245
One button alone reaches only a line.

15
00:00:54.245 --> 00:00:58.372
But a pair reaches the whole plane: u and w

16
00:00:58.372 --> 00:01:02.040
u and s, w and s, and every other pair.

17
00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.157
Here is a puzzle.

18
00:01:04.157 --> 00:01:08.729
Can three buttons, no two of them parallel

19
00:01:08.729 --> 00:01:10.703
still be wasteful?

20
00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.470
Pause and think.

21
00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:23.280
Vectors are independent when the only combination

22
00:01:23.359 --> 00:01:26.362
that gives zero has every amount zero.

23
00:01:26.362 --> 00:01:28.733
Otherwise they are dependent

24
00:01:28.812 --> 00:01:31.341
and one of them is a combination

25
00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:32.527
of the others.

26
00:01:32.877 --> 00:01:36.409
Put the vectors in the columns of a matrix.

27
00:01:36.492 --> 00:01:38.874
A combination that gives zero

28
00:01:38.956 --> 00:01:41.174
is then a nullspace vector

29
00:01:41.256 --> 00:01:44.378
so the columns are independent exactly

30
00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.171
when there are no free variables

31
00:01:47.171 --> 00:01:48.157
r equals n.

32
00:01:48.737 --> 00:01:53.310
The drone has rank two and four columns

33
00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.567
dependent.

34
00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:59.140
Here is one relation in the flat plane.

35
00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.713
Minus two u, then minus v, then plus w

36
00:02:03.713 --> 00:02:07.257
the path closes, back at zero.

37
00:02:07.607 --> 00:02:11.956
And another: u, then minus v, then plus s

38
00:02:11.956 --> 00:02:14.027
back at zero again.

39
00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.615
A dependence is a closed

40
00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:18.790
loop of the vectors.

41
00:02:18.893 --> 00:02:22.103
These are the special solutions

42
00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:23.967
of lecture seven.

43
00:02:24.547 --> 00:02:26.128
Three quick facts.

44
00:02:26.215 --> 00:02:28.674
A set that contains the zero

45
00:02:28.762 --> 00:02:31.133
vector is always dependent

46
00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:34.031
give the zero vector amount one.

47
00:02:34.119 --> 00:02:36.226
More than m vectors in R

48
00:02:36.314 --> 00:02:38.334
m are always dependent

49
00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:42.110
so in our flat plane any three arrows are

50
00:02:42.197 --> 00:02:45.095
and four buttons in R three could

51
00:02:45.183 --> 00:02:47.027
never be independent.

52
00:02:47.377 --> 00:02:50.615
And two vectors are dependent exactly

53
00:02:50.702 --> 00:02:53.852
when one is a multiple of the other

54
00:02:53.852 --> 00:02:55.777
they lie on one line.

55
00:02:56.357 --> 00:03:00.537
So is dependence just two parallel vectors?

56
00:03:00.537 --> 00:03:00.926
No.

57
00:03:00.926 --> 00:03:04.329
No two of u, v and w are parallel

58
00:03:04.329 --> 00:03:08.023
yet w is two u plus v: one step of u

59
00:03:08.023 --> 00:03:12.301
another, then one of v, lands exactly on w.

60
00:03:12.301 --> 00:03:14.926
For three or more vectors

61
00:03:14.926 --> 00:03:18.717
test with the rank, not two at a time.

62
00:03:19.067 --> 00:03:22.805
And dependent does not mean every vector

63
00:03:22.898 --> 00:03:25.795
is a combination of the others.

64
00:03:25.795 --> 00:03:29.813
In an ordinary plane, take a equal to one

65
00:03:29.813 --> 00:03:32.429
zero, b equal to two, zero

66
00:03:32.429 --> 00:03:34.858
and c equal to zero, one.

67
00:03:34.858 --> 00:03:38.783
They are dependent, because b is twice a.

68
00:03:38.783 --> 00:03:42.427
But c is not a combination of a and b.

69
00:03:43.007 --> 00:03:45.364
The span of some vectors is the

70
00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.720
set of all their combinations.

71
00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:51.141
The column space is the span of the columns

72
00:03:51.141 --> 00:03:54.258
all four buttons span the drone's plane

73
00:03:54.258 --> 00:03:56.386
and so do just two of them.

74
00:03:56.386 --> 00:03:59.047
Spanning says nothing about waste.

75
00:03:59.397 --> 00:04:01.778
And always name the space.

76
00:04:01.778 --> 00:04:03.976
u and v span the plane

77
00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:07.090
but not all of R three: one, one

78
00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:09.105
one is off the plane

79
00:04:09.105 --> 00:04:12.677
because one minus one plus one is one

80
00:04:12.677 --> 00:04:13.593
not zero.

81
00:04:13.593 --> 00:04:16.341
Add one, one, one to u and v

82
00:04:16.341 --> 00:04:20.004
the matrix of the three has rank three

83
00:04:20.004 --> 00:04:22.477
so they span all of space.

84
00:04:23.057 --> 00:04:26.084
So: vectors are independent when only

85
00:04:26.166 --> 00:04:28.784
the zero combination gives zero

86
00:04:28.784 --> 00:04:31.156
for the columns of a matrix

87
00:04:31.156 --> 00:04:32.547
when r equals n.

88
00:04:32.547 --> 00:04:35.410
Dependence is a loop back to zero

89
00:04:35.492 --> 00:04:37.537
and it can happen with no

90
00:04:37.619 --> 00:04:39.337
two vectors parallel.

91
00:04:39.687 --> 00:04:42.748
The span is all combinations

92
00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:47.393
and any two buttons span the drone's plane.

93
00:04:47.393 --> 00:04:48.554
Your turn

94
00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:52.249
can two vectors ever span R three?

95
00:04:52.249 --> 00:04:55.944
In part two: a basis, coordinates

96
00:04:55.944 --> 00:04:57.527
and dimension.
